Description: Maps floodplains and unconfined valley bottoms from a digital
    elevation model and a stream network with the Valley Confinement
    Algorithm (VCA), keeping ground that is gentle, near a stream in both
    straight-line and slope-weighted distance, and low relative to it. It
    classifies terrain and does not simulate floods, so its output is a
    screening map, not a field-validated floodplain. Fetches an elevation
    model for an area, maps preset flood levels, and attributes one
    floodplain to each watercourse that shares it, carrying per-reach flags
    onto the ground beside each reach. Ported from the bcfishpass lateral
    habitat pipeline (Python) with origins in the USDA VCA Toolbox and
    BlueGeo. Under active development.
